cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FVQual in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "FVQual: a 3D unstructured finite-volume hydrodynamic and water-quality model"
abstract: >-
  FVQual solves three-dimensional hydrostatic free-surface flow and multispecies
  water quality on unstructured tri-quad meshes with terrain-following sigma
  layers, using explicit finite-volume kernels and a declarative multispecies
  reaction engine. It is a HydroCouple 2.0 model component and a successor to
  the laterally averaged CE-QUAL-W2 model.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0-alpha.1
repository-code: "https://github.com/hydrocouple/FVQual"
url: "https://hydrocouple.org/projects/fvqual"
authors:
  - family-names: Buahin
    given-names: Caleb
keywords:
  - hydrodynamics
  - water quality
  - finite volume
  - unstructured mesh
  - reservoir modeling
  - UGRID
  - HydroCouple
references:
  - type: software
    title: "CE-QUAL-W2: A Two-Dimensional, Laterally Averaged, Hydrodynamic and Water Quality Model"
    license: MIT
    repository-code: "https://github.com/CE-QUAL-W2-ERDC/CE-QUAL-W2"
    url: "https://www.cequalw2.org/"
    notes: >-
      Physical formulations in FVQual are reimplemented from the CE-QUAL-W2
      theory manual; see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.
    authors:
      - name: "Environmental Laboratory, Engineer Research and Development Center, U.S. Army Corps of Engineers"
      - name: "Portland State University Water Quality Research Group"
